{
  "version": 1,
  "contract": [
    "Shared by scripts/cutover/probe/fpm-engine.php, php artisan cutover:smoke --engine-only --json and the controller's Python live config module.",
    "PHP prints route_values raw; Python builds the same values from bootstrap/cache/config.php and computes route_sha256. PHP never computes the route hash.",
    "Engine: the url scheme of the default connection when url is a non-empty string (aliases mysql2, postgres, postgresql, sqlite3, mssql), else its driver.",
    "Allowlist: database.default; database.connections holds the default connection and, when the engine is mysql, mysql_cache_locks, mysql_queue_worker and mysql_scheduling_cache (null when absent); database.repro_leftover_transactions; cache.default; cache.stores.default (the default store); cache.stores.scheduling; queue.default; driver, connection and table of every queue connection (only the keys present); app.key_sha256 (lowercase hex SHA-256 of the UTF-8 key, null when the key is null). A missing value is null.",
    "Passwords: every key named exactly password, at any depth, is replaced by password_set, which is false for null or the empty string and true otherwise. A map holding both password and password_set is refused. A url that carries a password is refused by the PHP probes.",
    "Canonical form: every array is an object with string keys (a JSON list becomes the object of its indexes); JSON with sorted keys, separators , and :, ASCII escapes, no NaN or infinity; route_sha256 is the lowercase hex SHA-256 of those bytes.",
    "On the lane this file belongs at scripts/cutover/production/testdata/route-hash-vectors.json; on the release D branch it lives here."
  ],
